n  rename or add new quality settings under  edit project settings and quality all  you have to do is create a drop down  menu in your game with the same amount  of  quality levels as what's in your project  settings and then call set quality level  on drop down value changed i watched  this tutorial by brachis i'm sure a lot  of you if you watch a lot of game dare  tutorials will know who he is wonderful  please watch that if you'd like to find  out more about how to create a settings  menu in unity description down below  link down below in description okay  here's the bonus one for you  number 11 there will be bugs don't panic  when working with a game that wasn't  built with performance or longevity in  mind there will come a time  where fixing one bug will just start to  create more so when i began improving  this  game i had grand visions of including  new sections to it new levels  adding new mechanics and features  and that simply just was not attainable  even though i was able to add one new  feature of a webcam  and update some of the designs on  certain aspects such as the doors  i  had to ultimately abandon my  hopes and dreams of including much more  content to the game itself and after i  had worked my little butt off for three  weeks  updating this game's performance and  released it letting people know about it  on social media  i  then realized that there was a pc  specific game breaking bug  and not gonna lie i was  so  [Music]  tired  i think i just i'd worked really hard  and then to find out that the game  couldn't even be completed by some  people  was just a kind of kick in the face to  make matters worse because it was pc  specific it didn't happen on my pc so i  had to  give the potential fixed builds to  someone whose pc  did have the bug it took longer to do  that one bug than to update the  performance of the whole game it was  infuriating but  that is game development for you it's a  fickle process but it is challenging and  it is really